<title>UK: EMU to cost Euro financial sector 16 bln stg - CIB.</title>
<headline>EMU to cost Euro financial sector 16 bln stg - CIB.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Union (EMU) will cost European financial services sector companies at least 16 billion stg, with banks alone having to pay 9.7 billion, says the latest estimate by the UK Chartered Institute of Bankers.</p>
<p>The CIB said the figures, produced by business consultancy Cap Gemini, were based on publicly available data and information from top financial institutions and assume that the single currency will be introduced with a dual currency operation period, during which banks will need systems to handle both the existing national currency and the Euro. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
